Scope, as the card asks:
- one operator command that runs both at-rest side-copy rewrites (`migrateSideCopies` and `migrateArchivedSideCopies`), on whatever surface the CLI already uses for one-off data rewrites;
- a dry run by default and an explicit apply;
- a per-object option;
- the counts it wrote, in its report.

It also settles the rewrite's name, adds a test and documents the command.
